# Design / SLD ≠ Proposal surface

## Locked product decision (2026-07-21)

- **Do NOT** embed Design Studio layout, roof map, panel placement, or SLD into the customer **proposal** experience (tabs, share link, or proposal PDF blocks) as the long-term default.
- Proposals stay a **simple commercial offer** (price, savings, terms, branding). Keep them easy for installers who only sell quotes.
- **Design** and **SLD** are separate product capabilities. They may sit under Project / Design Hub, with their **own** share links and **separate** print/PDF outputs.
- Future **subscription plans / feature categories** will turn Design and/or SLD on or off. Coupling them into proposal would force complexity onto every tier and every “proposal-only” user.

## When building later

- Prefer: Proposal link (quote) + optional Design pack link + optional SLD pack link.
- Optional cross-links from Project Hub are fine; do not require Design/SLD UI inside proposal presets/renderers.
- Pricing snapshots stay on the proposal; design versions stay on the project (`project_site_layouts` / panel layouts / SLD assets).
- If a roadmap item says “add site layout block to proposal PDF”, treat it as superseded by this rule unless the user explicitly re-opens the decision.

## Remind the user

When starting Design↔customer delivery, Phase 5 integration, or subscription feature gating work, remind: Design and SLD remain separate from proposal; proposal stays simple and subscription-safe.
